`reconstruction_error` converts a list or a DataFrame to an array, so it returns an array instead of failing or returning a DataFrame or Series. `TrajectoryResult` and `TrajectoryResult.from_grid` raise when `times` does not have one entry per time point, which used to give wrong speeds and AUCs silently. Curvature and turning angle are NaN where the path stops, since a zero-length step has no direction: `trajectory_curvature(method="cosine")` used to read one repeated point as a right angle divided by machine epsilon (about 7e15), and `trajectory_turning_angle` as a straight step. `trajectory_curvature(method="gradient")` set curvature to 0 wherever `|v|^3 < 1e-8`, a threshold that depends on the data's scale and sampling rate, so a slow path (about 1e-3 per sample) read as straight; it is now NaN only where the velocity is exactly zero. The trajectory summaries of `evaluate_embedding` and `DimReduction.score` propagate NaN like `TrajectoryResult` instead of skipping it, so one repeated point gives the same NaN mean curvature from both.
